<title>USA: Regulators approve Unicom unit plant sale.</title>
<headline>Regulators approve Unicom unit plant sale.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unicom Corp said Monday the Illinois Commerce Commission approved the sale of two coal-fired power plants in Indiana and Illinois owned by its Commonwealth Edison Co subsidiary.</p>
<p>ComEd said it sold the State Line Generating Station in Hammond, Indiana, to a unit of Southern Co for $64 million and the Kincaid Generating Station in Kincaid, Illinois, to a division of Dominion Resources Inc for $186 million.</p>
<p>ComEd will have exclusive rights to the electricity generated at the plants under a 15-year Power Purchase Agreement, Unicom said.</p>
<p>Unicom is a utility holding company.</p>
<p>Its shares were off 5/8 Monday at 19-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
